\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Uncontrolled Langevin back-noising sweep ($\gamma \in [0, 3.0]$ across $\text  {SC-CFG}\in \{1,2,3,4\}$, 56 runs, $n=2$ seeds/cell, $M=1{,}000$ samples/seed) on ELF-B. \textbf  {(a)} Increasing $\gamma $ drives raw Gen-PPL monotonically below the OpenWebText reference line ($17.18$; reaching $16.70$ at $\gamma =3.0, \text  {SC-CFG}=3.0$), but \textbf  {(b)} plotting the same 56 runs against per-sample entropy $H_{\mathrm  {ps}}$ reveals that all four guidance scales collapse onto a shared trajectory (quadratic $R^2 = 0.989$) driven by entropy contraction.}}{16}{figure.caption.26}\protected@file@percent }
